Package: broom
Version: @VERSION@-1
Architecture: amd64
Maintainer: Broom maintainers <maintainers@example.invalid>
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: libc6 (>= 2.34), libstdc++6 (>= 11), libgtk-3-0 | libgtk-3-0t64, libglib2.0-0 | libglib2.0-0t64, liblzma5, systemd, pkexec | policykit-1, polkitd | policykit-1
Section: utils
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://melaine-iceberg.github.io/broom/
Description: Safe, reversible cache cleaner for Linux desktops
 Broom scans declared cache locations, previews the results, and moves
 files to a per-user quarantine so a clean can be undone. The optional
 system helper cleans APT or DNF package caches and the systemd journal
 after one Polkit authorization.
 .
 The package installs the desktop entry, hicolor icons, the
 broom-system-helper and its Polkit policy. Removing the package does not
 delete the user's quarantine, settings or clean history under
 $XDG_DATA_HOME/Broom.
